+<body>
+<main id="m1_reframing-entrepreneurship-and-going-solo" class="composition" data-composition-id="m1_reframing-entrepreneurship-and-going-solo" data-start="0" data-width="1920" data-height="1080" data-fps="30" data-duration="77.5">
+<header class="chrome"><span>Entrepreneur Accelerator · 01</span><span class="brand-rule"></span></header>
+<section id="beat-01" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-01" data-track-index="0" data-start="0" data-duration="9.2" data-end="9.2"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">Reframing Entrepreneurship and Going Solo</div><h1 class="headline">It Doesn’t Have to Begin with a <span class="gold">Huge Leap</span></h1><div class="experiment">It can begin small.</div><p class="narration">When people hear the word "entrepreneur," they often imagine someone launching a startup, raising money, or making a huge leap into the unknown. But for most people, entrepreneurship begins much smaller than that.</p></div></section>
+<section id="beat-02" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-02" data-track-index="0" data-start="9.2" data-duration="10.8" data-end="20"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">Start where you are</div><h2 class="headline">One Small Experiment</h2><div class="cards"><div class="card">Side project</div><div class="card">Freelance client</div><div class="card">Workshop</div><div class="card">Digital product</div><div class="card">Service</div></div><p class="narration">It might begin as a side project, a freelance client, a workshop you offer, a digital product you test, or a service you share with people you already know. In other words, entrepreneurship often begins as a series of experiments.</p></div></section>
+<section id="beat-03" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-03" data-track-index="0" data-start="20" data-duration="16" data-end="36"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">AI accelerates · humans make it work</div><h2 class="headline">Move Faster · Stay Human</h2><div class="split"><div class="panel"><h3>AI Can Help</h3><p>Ideas · offers · research · language · repetitive work</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>People Make It Matter</h3><p>Judgment · trust · relationships · real problem-solving</p></div></div><p class="narration">In an AI-accelerated world, this kind of experimentation is even more accessible. AI tools can help you brainstorm ideas, draft offers, organize research, refine marketing language, and streamline repetitive work. But AI doesn't replace the human elements that make solo work successful: judgment, trust, relationships, and the ability to solve real problems for real people.</p></div></section>
+<section id="beat-04" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-04" data-track-index="0" data-start="36" data-duration="8" data-end="44"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">The track promise</div><h2 class="headline">AI Doesn’t Avoid the Work<br><span class="gold">It Reduces the Friction</span></h2><div class="cards"><div class="card">Move faster</div><div class="card">Think clearly</div><div class="card">Test ideas</div></div><p class="narration">That's what this track is about. Not using AI to avoid the work, but using it to help you move faster, think more clearly, and test ideas with less friction.</p></div></section>
+<section id="beat-05" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-05" data-track-index="0" data-start="44" data-duration="11.5" data-end="55.5"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">Your pathway</div><h2 class="headline">From Idea to Launch Plan</h2><div class="path"><span class="node">Design</span><span class="arrow">→</span><span class="node">Compare</span><span class="arrow">→</span><span class="node">Package</span><span class="arrow">→</span><span class="node">Reach out</span><span class="arrow">→</span><span class="node gold">30–90 days</span></div><p class="narration">In the modules ahead, you'll design a side hustle or solo-work experiment, compare freelancing, consulting, and fractional work, package your first offer, draft simple outreach, and create a launch plan for the next 30 to 90 days.</p></div></section>
+<section id="beat-06" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-06" data-track-index="0" data-start="55.5" data-duration="10" data-end="65.5"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">Release the pressure</div><h2 class="headline">You Don’t Need a Forever Business</h2><p class="sub">You need the willingness to run <strong class="gold">one smart experiment</strong> and see what you learn.</p><p class="narration">You don't need to know whether you want to become a full-time entrepreneur. You don't need to know your forever business. You only need to be willing to run one smart experiment and see what you learn.</p></div></section>
+<section id="beat-07" class="clip" data-beat-id="beat-07" data-track-index="0" data-start="65.5" data-duration="12" data-end="77.5"><div class="scene"><div class="eyebrow">Keep asking</div><h2 class="headline">What Can I Test?</h2><div class="question"><div class="q">One useful thing</div><div class="q">One real group</div><div class="q">One realistic way</div></div><div class="resolve">How can AI help me test it faster?</div><p class="narration">As you move through this track, keep asking yourself: what is one useful thing I can offer, to one real group of people, in one realistic way—and how can AI help me test that faster?</p></div></section>
+</main>
